---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---
<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" draft={true}>
  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> TBD<br /><strong>Last updated:</strong> July 2026</p>

  <h2>1. What We Collect</h2>
  <p>When you submit a review, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Review content:</strong> Company name, headline answer, dimension ratings, story text, and optional identity lens tag.</li>
    <li><strong>Email address (optional):</strong> Only if you choose to provide one, stored separately from your review, for removal requests only.</li>
    <li><strong>Removal token:</strong> A random token returned to you after submission. This is the primary way to identify your review for removal. We store only a one-way hash of the token — the plaintext is shown once and cannot be recovered.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>When you join our waitlist, we collect your email address.</p>
  <p>
    Our infrastructure providers (hosting, CDN) keep standard server access logs, including IP address, for a short period set by them. We do not control the retention window and we do not retain copies of these logs ourselves. We do not use server logs to identify reviewers.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What We Do NOT Collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Work email addresses for verification</li>
    <li>SSO or single sign-on credentials</li>
    <li>GPS location or precise geolocation</li>
    <li>Employer-verifiable information (exact hire/leave dates, department names, employee IDs)</li>
    <li>Any information that could directly identify you as the reviewer</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How We Use Your Data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Review data</strong> is aggregated into company-level scores displayed on the Service. Individual reviews are never attributed to a specific person.</li>
    <li><strong>Identity lens tags</strong> are used to compute lens-specific aggregate scores. They are only displayed when enough reviews exist for that lens at that company to protect anonymity.</li>
    <li><strong>Email addresses</strong> are used solely to process removal requests. They are never published, sold, or shared with third parties.</li>
    <li><strong>Waitlist emails</strong> are used to send product updates. You can unsubscribe at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Data Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Review submissions are received by our server infrastructure and stored in our database for moderation. Approved reviews are included in the aggregated scores displayed on the Service. Individual review records are retained for as long as they remain approved and part of the dataset, or until the reviewer requests removal.
  </p>

  <h2>4a. Data Retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Approved reviews</strong> are retained as long as they remain part of the published dataset or until the reviewer requests removal.</li>
    <li><strong>Removal tokens</strong> (hashed) and optional contact emails are retained as long as the associated review exists.</li>
    <li><strong>Rejected reviews</strong> are deleted promptly after rejection.</li>
    <li><strong>Waitlist emails</strong> are retained until you unsubscribe.</li>
    <li><strong>Server access logs</strong> (maintained by our infrastructure providers, not by us) are retained for a short period determined by those providers. We do not retain copies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or share personal data with third parties. Aggregated, anonymized score data may be referenced in public reporting or research, but never in a way that could identify individual reviewers.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Removal (with token):</strong> After submitting a review, you receive a one-time removal token. To remove your review, visit <a href="/remove" class="text-coral hover:text-coral/80 underline">belongary.com/remove</a> and enter your token. This is the primary method and works regardless of whether you provided an email.</li>
    <li><strong>Removal (with email):</strong> If you provided an email address during submission and have lost your token, email us from that address at <strong>support@belongary.com</strong>. We can use it to locate your submission.</li>
    <li><strong>If you have neither:</strong> We cannot verify ownership of an anonymous review without the token or the email address used at submission. The token cannot be recovered once lost.</li>
    <li><strong>Waitlist removal:</strong> Email <strong>support@belongary.com</strong> to be removed from the waitlist.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
  <p>
    Belongary does not use tracking cookies, analytics pixels, or third-party advertising scripts. We may use essential cookies for basic site functionality (e.g., form submission state).
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Belongary is not intended for use by anyone under the age of 18. We do not knowingly collect information from minors.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy as needed. Changes will be reflected in the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions? Email <strong>privacy@belongary.com</strong>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
